# Interaction-safe space (Medora)

Use tokens from `src/lib/asset/style/interaction-safe-space.css` (imported in `layout.css`).

## Formula

On any ancestor with `overflow` other than `visible`:

`pad = max(R, L, S, B) + G + ε`

| Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| R | `outline-width + outline-offset` (`--wash-state-ring`) |
| L | Hover/focus lift (`--wash-state-lift`, e.g. 2px) |
| S | Focus/hover shadow footprint (`--wash-state-shadow`) |
| B | Half border-width change on focus; keep **0** with stable `border-width` |
| G | Dropdown gap (`--wash-dropdown-gap`) |
| ε | 1px (`--wash-state-epsilon`) |

Computed token: `--wash-interaction-inset`.

Stacked fields: `gap >= pad` (use class `wash-form-stack`).

Scroll containers with fields: `scroll-padding >= pad`.

## Apply

- **WashDialog** body: `wash-dialog-scroll-body` or `wash-dialog-form-column` (already on shell).
- **Inner dialog forms**: `wash-form-stack` on field column; inner `overflow-y-auto` gets auto padding via `:has()` or `wash-interaction-scroll`.
- **Tables**: keep `menzies-table-scroll` on table body; do not add form padding there. Row menus portaled (fixed), not clipped dropdowns.
- **Opt out**: `wash-interaction-scroll-opt-out` on a scroller that must stay flush.

## Do not

- Put `overflow-auto` on a form column with `pr-1` or zero padding only; rings will clip.
- Use `class:` on `WashButton` for loading; use `loading` prop.
- Rely on daisyUI `dropdown` inside `overflow-auto` without portal; use `measureDropdownPlacement` + fixed panel (SearchSelect / WashSelect / row menus).
